Azure Subscription

Whenever we are creating any resource we need Subscription, Resource Group and Location.

An Azure subscription is a logical container and a binding agreement with Microsoft that grants you access to, manages, and bills for your cloud resources

An Azure resource group is a logical container that holds related cloud services and infrastructure for an application or solution

PowerShell Commands:
> Get-AzSubscription # info about subscription
> Get-azresourcegroup # info about resourcegroup
# to get info about anything use get

Bash Commands:
$ az account list # subscription details
$ az account list --output table # subscription details in a table format
$ az group list -- output table # resource group details in a table format
$ az group show --name "groupname"


Azure Subscription and Resource Groups.

Azure Subscription is an active agreement between Microsoft and its users. This agreement provides users the needed access to avail the services and resources offered by Microsoft Azure.
An azure account can be associated with multiple subscriptions for separate billings based on user defined criteria.

Azure Subscription is equivalent to AWS Organization.

A resource group in Azure is simply a collection of related Azure assets or Azure services that belong to an application or workload together
800,000 resources can be in a resource group
