Understanding Azure Architecture

Understanding Azure Resource Manager 
When any tool is used to take actions on Azure resources, the Azure Resource Manager API handles that request. The API passes the request to the Resource Manager, which authenticates and authorizes it. The Resource Manager then routes the request to the appropriate service 

Azure Portal, Azure Powershell, Azure  CLI, Rest CLients -> Azure Resource Manager -> Authentication -> Azure Resource Manager -> Azure services -> creates/deletes/changes

-> Azure Resource Manager(ARM) is the deployment and management service for Azure resources.
-> Using this service, users can create, update and delete resources in their subscription
-> It offers features such as access control, auditing and tagging to secure and organize resources after deployment.

